+# GPU Node Pool & NVMe caching example (instructions)
+
+This file documents example approaches — adapt to your cloud provider:
+
+- GKE: create a node pool with GPU accelerator type (e.g., A100), taints and nodeSelector labels; use local SSDs for NVMe cache (local SSD disk).
+- EKS: create an ASG for GPU instances; use a StorageClass backed by NVMe (instance storage or high-performance EBS).
+- AKS: use GPU node pools and enable ephemeral disks or attach high-perf managed disks for model caches.
+
+Recommendations:
+- Label nodes with node.kubernetes.io/gpu=true and cloud-specific GPU labels, then set nodeSelector in Helm charts.
+- Use a CSI driver that supports local NVMe caching, or deploy a sidecar cache (e.g., node-local cache) to stage model shards.
+- Enable cluster autoscaler to scale GPU pools based on pod demands.
